A||||7||AkursedX||Blueprinting||||5||
Z||000000||AkursedX||05-21-2001||09:49 PM||||Ok, could someone tell me exactly what is done when an engine is "blueprinted"?  <P>Thanks in advance  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Scott||05-22-2001||12:49 AM||||Basically everthing is checked wtih various calipers and assembled for optimum clearances.  For example, if one cylinder is bored just slightly larger than the rest (within a few thousanths of an inch), the piston with the largest diameter is installed into this cylinder.  In this way the clearances are tighter, making for a more efficient engine.  A similar process is used for all components throughout engine assembly.  BTW, if the engine is balanced, the components are weighed and assembled so that the weights of the piston/rod units are very close to the opposing unit accross the crankshaft.  These procedures can make noticable increases in power and longevity of a motor, but they are a pain in the *** to do, and therefore are expensive.<BR>HTH,<BR>Scott    ||||reg||3
Z||000002||S. Goertzen||05-22-2001||01:29 AM||||Blueprinting is when the engine is built EXACTLY to the factory blueprint or specifications. When an engine is produced, it isn't perfect. For example, a 2.5L in the Fiero is actually 2.47L, therefore boring the cylinders is required to achieve an actual 2.5L. Balancing the rotating assembly includes the crankshaft, connecting rods, flywheel, and balancer on the front of the engine. As mentioned, this is good for horsepower gains, but combined with polishing the crankshaft and connecting rods (or buying aftermarket units that have already been improved) is also good for a higher redline. Polishing them basically involves removing the casting defects, which helps eliminate hot spots, making things stronger. Hope that this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000003||AkursedX||05-22-2001||02:49 PM||||Ok, you guys answered that question for me.  Thank you very much  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <BR>Now one more question.  could somebody give a general estimate for how much both balancing and blueprinting would cost, for a 2.8?  <P>||||reg||1
